          "anchorId": "decepticars",
          "heading": "Decepticars",
          "body": "The Decepticars are the highway’s premier performance artists of the visual lie. While most clans signal their intent through their body style, this group operates on a platform of pure, unadulterated bait-and-switch. To a Decepticar, the exterior of a vehicle is merely a costume designed to liven up the commute through psychological warfare. They thrive on the \"Uncanny Valley\" of performance, where the physics of the car and the behavior of the driver are in a constant, confusing divorce..\n\nDetecting a member of this clan requires you to ignore your eyes and trust your speedometer. They are the glitch in the highway matrix.\n\nThe Decepticars represent the ultimate subversion of expectations within the Rush Hour Villains ecosystem. They aren't just drivers; they are masters of a \"wolf in sheep’s clothing\" (or vice versa) strategy that leaves surrounding commuters in a state of perpetual bewilderment. By weaponizing the mismatch between aesthetic and ability, they ensure that no one on the road can ever truly \"read the room.\" They are the highway’s reminder that you should never judge a villain by their spoiler—because the most dangerous threat is the one you completely miscalculated.",
