          "anchorId": "showtime",
          "heading": "Showtime",
          "body": "The Showtime clan operates on a single, deafening frequency: \"Look at me, Hear me, and Feel my bass in your dental work.\" To a Showtimer, a vehicle is not a mode of transportation—it is a mobile Broadway stage, a rolling nightclub, and a 4-wheeled billboard all rolled into one. They don’t just enter traffic; they premiere. If their commute hasn't triggered at least three car alarms and caused a localized power surge with their underglow, they consider the trip a box-office failure.\n\n​You won't need to look for a Showtimer; they will find your ears, your eyes, and your vibration-sensitive steering wheel long before you see their bumper.\n\nThe Showtime clan represents the ultimate extroverts of the Rush Hour Villains universe. While the Bubble Brigade is unaware of your existence, the Showtimers are desperate for you to acknowledge theirs. They turn the mundane commute into a forced participatory experience, ensuring that even if you’re stuck in gridlock, you’re stuck at a concert you didn't buy tickets for. They are the highway’s loudest reminder that some people don't just want to get to point B—they want to make sure everyone at point A, B, and C knows exactly how they got there.",
          "imagePath": "clans/showtime.png",
          "imagePosition": "left",
